{"abstract":[{"text":"The pedal-type simple type is used to distinguish types of pedal directions. The start value indicates the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"start of a damper pedal, while the sostenuto value indicates the start of a sostenuto pedal. The other values","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can be used with either the damper or sostenuto pedal. The soft pedal is not included here because there is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no special symbol or graphic used for it beyond what can be specified with words and bracket elements.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"title":"MXLPedal.Kind","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Kind"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLPedalV4KindO","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"enum","roleHeading":"Enumeration","extendedModule":"IvorMXL","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Kind"}]},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Enumeration-Cases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/Kind-swift.enum\/change","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/Kind-swift.enum\/continue","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/Kind-swift.enum\/discontinue","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/Kind-swift.enum\/resume","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/Kind-swift.enum\/sostenuto","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/Kind-swift.enum\/start","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/Kind-swift.enum\/stop"],"title":"Enumeration Cases"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/Kind-swift.enum\/Equatable-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpedal\/kind-swift.enum"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Kind","kind":"identifier"}]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The change, continue, discontinue, and resume types are used when the line attribute is yes. The change type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indicates a pedal lift and retake indicated with an inverted V marking. The continue type allows more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"precise formatting across system breaks and for more complex pedaling lines. The discontinue type indicates"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the end of a pedal line that does not include the explicit lift represented by the stop type. The resume"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type indicates the start of a pedal line that does not include the downstroke represented by the start"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type. It can be used when a line resumes after being discontinued, or to start a pedal line that is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"preceded by a text or symbol representation of the pedal."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/Kind-swift.enum","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPedal/Kind-swift.enum/sostenuto":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"MXLPedal.Kind.sostenuto","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpedal\/kind-swift.enum\/sostenuto","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/Kind-swift.enum\/sostenuto","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sostenuto","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The start of a sostenuto pedal.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/s8CopyableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Copyable"},"doc://IvorMXL/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"title":"Swift.SendableMetatype","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPedal/Kind-swift.enum/change":{"abstract":[{"text":"A pedal lift and retake, indicated with an inverted V marking.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLPedal.Kind.change","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpedal\/kind-swift.enum\/change","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"change"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/Kind-swift.enum\/change"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPedal/Kind-swift.enum/continue":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"MXLPedal.Kind.continue","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpedal\/kind-swift.enum\/continue","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/Kind-swift.enum\/continue","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"`continue`","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A continuation of a pedal line, allowing more precise formatting across system breaks.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPedal":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpedal","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The pedal type represents piano pedal marks, including damper and sostenuto pedal marks. The line attribute is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"yes if pedal lines are used. The sign attribute is yes if Ped, Sost, and * signs are used. For compatibility"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with older versions, the sign attribute is yes by default if the line attribute is no, and is no by default if"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the line attribute is yes. If the sign attribute is set to yes and the type is start or sostenuto, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"abbreviated attribute is yes if the short P and S signs are used, and no if the full Ped and Sost signs are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"used. It is no by default. Otherwise the abbreviated attribute is ignored. The alignment attributes are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ignored if the sign attribute is no."}],"title":"MXLPedal","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPedal"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPedal"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPedal/Kind-swift.enum/discontinue":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpedal\/kind-swift.enum\/discontinue","kind":"symbol","title":"MXLPedal.Kind.discontinue","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/Kind-swift.enum\/discontinue","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"discontinue"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The end of a pedal line that does not include the explicit lift represented by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stop"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.